  "text": "Question six. Walk me through diagnosing a sudden eight percent drop in daily active users, D A U. First: is it real? A logging change, a broken pipeline, or a holiday can make that shape on its own. Then, is it broad or narrow? Say the app had a hundred thousand daily users. Split by platform, iPhone and web barely moved. Android lost seventy-five hundred of the eight thousand. Then, what changed, and when? Android release five point two went out that morning. Last, internal or external: a competitor's launch looks different from a bug of your own.\n\nQuestion seven. How do you decide whether a change is signal or noise? Measure the normal swing first. This metric moves about three percent on an ordinary day, so a two percent dip sits well inside its band. In eight simulated weeks with nothing wrong, twenty-four days moved further than that. A real shift persists for days, clears the band, and shows up in related metrics too. Next, testing a change, and what to do when you can't.",
